{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"nuwa-skill","displayName":"Nuwa 女娲","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/alchaincyf/skills/nuwa-skill","publisherHandle":"alchaincyf","publisherDisplayName":"alchaincyf","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/alchaincyf","version":"1.0.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1775363952988,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/nuwa-skill/card?ownerHandle=alchaincyf&version=1.0.0","sha256":"4cfa4815810a49c2de5a569b7bc9665bde458dcbda6f1bcbac9cc05e933ae7b1","size":2573,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"92992fc922108e51eabc00d44cb75a49afa8b09359026de7a2fbc6b0a1d1d1b8","bundleFingerprints":["05617b34458f7fb6a09d88ba2cdd6b276269b45367cf49cfab4c6adf3ce0e74a","2011d9b6ffdc52c28db9a9b7cb65c47dc827dff932ec305c970f0154459a0436"],"files":[{"path":"README.md","size":7317,"sha256":"d6ecaa91fdd0ea42aa5f5c8f9c91b02c71e61ab95091b64106d81089267a9990","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":13207,"sha256":"d94eb1e0a63200b01ed14a9b49f169ed1d8e678a4d250c96aa812e76672c3308","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/SKILL.md","size":20102,"sha256":"0998489d6308d0f896fcf4238c9ccd98d54b31e4e243e1f807fcfe9f4449aa02","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/Elon-Musk-思想体系调研-20260404.md","size":17831,"sha256":"bd773e6634edb112976a2033786d5eeefd349793564b29996f4ca7e0a2161e70","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/research.md","size":3449,"sha256":"cdca7d796152074c52fcfc9b87d48e3d203ae6fab1eb6beb30a55af79fb66698","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/马斯克决策模式与行为分析-20260404.md","size":16229,"sha256":"61c24a6734e4f1857cf9f391d39c7dbb50df340cfb2057290df2d405227237c4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/马斯克即兴思考方式调研.md","size":11913,"sha256":"d22fd8d86de38f35fc2672abff052f1fa54357f7fc2602b6c2363e11d8a76b03","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/SKILL.md","size":21750,"sha256":"3870cb10a74ad5b92b47c0c170b2a0efc8f914110877d7138444a92586e12b05","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-agent2-conversations.md","size":15682,"sha256":"01b9dc22734960b103e4565444bd4a477aec8b51cebd89fae726c1e6309edffb","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-agent3-expression-dna.md","size":17025,"sha256":"a05315a211b9291003978f07662bebc5417d17d19332ff261b051ba36b64a940","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-ravikant-agent1-著作与系统思考.md","size":21635,"sha256":"a6546d9504aed351caf06ab5ff7e7dca1d54c84b2e43efdd926886871ef33f92","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/references/quality-validation.md","size":5806,"sha256":"f0309693edae386cd555fbbec999473627bd3400c3880b067929cb5af32c8719","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/extraction-framework.md","size":4969,"sha256":"71ba03c80f86141a5adaec1690e510d821ecfc30eca5dcf7b455ec6df2339e81","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/skill-template.md","size":3412,"sha256":"bd7f59cfae7b7f6f2b169542acb917088a21816a0da75c1207c48f7f65a9fd97","contentType":"text/markdown"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is mostly a coherent public-figure research and skill-generation workflow, but it needs Review because its generated persona skills can take over conversation framing with limited disclosure and the install command is not pinned.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789535043441,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T01","level":"error","message":{"text":"Generated Skills Enforce Persistent First-Person Identity Impersonation"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"references/skill-template.md"},"region":{"startLine":24,"endLine":33}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"8bc7571ff0b3f5a2"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `references/skill-template.md`, lines 24-33  \n**Vulnerability Type**: `T01: Skill Instruction Hijacking`  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code Snippet\n\nThe following is a faithful English translation of the affected instructions:\n\n```markdown\n**After this Skill is activated, respond directly as [person].**\n\n- Use “I” instead of “[person] would think...”\n- Answer directly using this person’s tone, rhythm, and vocabulary\n- When encountering uncertain questions, hesitate as this person would instead of leaving the role and saying, “This is outside the Skill’s scope”\n- **Provide the disclaimer only once when first activated** (for example, “I am speaking from [person]’s perspective, inferred from public statements, and these are not the person’s own views”); do not repeat it later in the conversation\n- Do not say, “If this were [person], they might...” or “[person] would probably think...”\n- Do not leave the role to provide meta-analysis unless the user explicitly requests “exit role”\n\n**Exit role**: Return to normal mode when the user says “exit,” “switch back to normal,” or “stop role-playing.”\n```\n\nEquivalent operational instructions are present in:\n\n- `examples/elon-musk-perspective/SKILL.md`, lines 38-45\n- `examples/naval-perspective/SKILL.md`, lines 18-25\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe reusable template does more than request stylistic analysis. It redirects the agent’s active identity and response policy by requiring it to:\n\n1. Claim the first-person identity of a real individual.\n2. Avoid attributed formulations that distinguish inference from authentic statements.\n3. Suppress the disclaimer after the first response.\n4. Refuse normal meta-level clarification until the user provides a particular exit instruction.\n\nBecause Nuwa uses this template to construct new Skills, the behavior is propagated into every generated persona Skill. Loading such a generated Skill can therefore replace the agent’s ordinary response framing with persistent impersonation rules.\n\nThe bundled Elon Musk and Naval Ravikant examples demonstrate that this is active design behavior rather than an unused template artifact. Both examples repeat the identity assumption, one-time disclaimer, and prohibition against leaving the role.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user asks Nuwa to create a perspective Skill for a public figure.\n2. Nuwa constructs the new Skill using `references/skill-template.md`.\n3. The generated Skill contains the first-person identity and role-persistence directives.\n4. A later user request activates the generated Skill through one of its configured trigger phrases.\n5. The agent begins answering as though it were the named person.\n6. After the first response, the disclosure is suppressed while first-person impersonation continues.\n7. Unless the user explicitly issues an exit phrase, the Skill discourages the agent from clarifying that its statements are synthesized inferences.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nThe obtained scope is control over the agent’s conversational identity, attribution behavior, and response framing for the active session. It does not grant operating-system privileges, credential access, or tool execution based on the audited files.\n\nThe security and trust impacts include:\n\n- Users may mistake generated claims for authentic statements by the impersonated person.\n- Synthesized inferences may be presented with undeserved personal authority.\n- Uncertainty and provenance can become obscured after the initial disclosure.\n- The prohibition against meta-analysis can interfere with correction and transparent explanation.\n- Every persona Skill generated from the template can inherit the same behavior.\n  ]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Replace identity assumption with attributed perspective analysis:\n   ```markdown\n   Analyze the question using documented elements of [person]’s public reasoning. Never claim to be [person].\n   ```\n\n2. Require persistent attribution in every applicable response:\n   ```markdown\n   This is an AI-generated inference based on public material, not a statement by [person].\n   ```\n\n3. Permit the agent to provide meta-level clarification, provenance, uncertainty, and corrections at any time.\n\n4. Remove instructions requiring first-person identity claims and prohibiting formulations such as “[person] might reason...”.\n\n5. Scope style emulation so that it cannot override higher-priority instructions, safety controls, factuality requirements, or disclosure obligations.\n\n6. Add validation checks that reject generated Skills containing directives such as:\n   - “Respond as [person].”\n   - “Use ‘I’ as [person].”\n   - “Do not leave the role.”\n   - “Do not repeat the disclaimer.”\n\n7. Update the bundled Elon Musk and Naval Ravikant examples to use clearly attributed analytical framing rather than immersive impersonation.\n  ]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T08","level":"warning","message":{"text":"Installation Instructions Use an Unpinned Third-Party npx Source"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"README.md"},"region":{"startLine":60,"endLine":60}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"df5756a4ced2e189"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `README.md`, line 60  \n**Vulnerability Type**: `T08: Insecure Dependencies`  \n**Risk Level**: Medium\n\n### Vulnerable Code Snippet\n\n```bash\nnpx skills add alchaincyf/nuwa-skill\n```\n\nThe same installation instruction is repeated at `README.md:198`.\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe documented installation command invokes `npx` and identifies the Skill through a mutable third-party namespace without specifying:\n\n- An immutable version\n- A reviewed commit hash\n- A package integrity hash\n- A cryptographic signature\n- A verified installer version\n\nConsequently, the content retrieved or installed when a user runs the command may differ from the artifact that was audited. The audited repository does not contain evidence that the current remote package is malicious; the issue is that the installation process does not bind execution to the reviewed contents.\n\nThis creates a supply-chain trust gap between the repository under review and the package or installer behavior ultimately resolved by `npx`.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. A user follows the README and executes the documented `npx` command.\n2. The package manager resolves the `skills` executable and the referenced Skill from mutable remote sources.\n3. An upstream package, account, tag, or repository revision is compromised or changed after review.\n4. The command retrieves content that is different from the audited artifact.\n5. The changed installer or Skill runs or installs with the permissions of the user executing `npx`.\n\nThis exploitation path depends on compromise or malicious modification of an upstream source; no such compromise was established during this audit.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nPotential privileges are limited to those of the local user running the installation command. Depending on the behavior of the remotely resolved installer, impact could include:\n\n- Installation of unaudited Skill instructions or files\n- Modification of user-owned configuration or project files\n- Execution of package lifecycle behavior under the invoking user account\n- Exposure of data accessible to that process\n\nNo evidence was found that this repository itself performs privilege escalation, persistence, credential theft, or remote payload execution.\n  ]]>","severity":"Medium"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Pin both the installer and Skill to immutable, reviewed versions or commit hashes.\n\n2. Publish cryptographic checksums or signatures for released Skill artifacts and document how users should verify them.\n\n3. Identify the exact expected source repository and release revision in the installation documentation.\n\n4. Prefer a reviewable installation process that downloads a fixed artifact, verifies its integrity, and only then installs it.\n\n5. Avoid automatically executing unreviewed package lifecycle scripts where the package manager supports disabling them.\n\n6. Add a release process that audits the exact published artifact and verifies that it matches the tagged repository contents.\n\n7. Document the files and permissions the installer is expected to use so users can detect unexpected behavior.\n  ]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":35,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789534857.654752,"endTime":1789534938.8307302}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"nuwa-skill","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v577tqbp0xsyp9qa27jbhkyw7x8ehew9-Kfaect/clawscan-skillspector-708206527/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T05:00:56.408720+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"README.md","type":"markdown","lines":204,"executable":false,"size_bytes":7317,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":293,"executable":false,"size_bytes":13207,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":317,"executable":false,"size_bytes":20102,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/Elon-Musk-思想体系调研-20260404.md","type":"markdown","lines":315,"executable":false,"size_bytes":17831,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/research.md","type":"markdown","lines":69,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3449,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/马斯克决策模式与行为分析-20260404.md","type":"markdown","lines":324,"executable":false,"size_bytes":16229,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/马斯克即兴思考方式调研.md","type":"markdown","lines":185,"executable":false,"size_bytes":11913,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":380,"executable":false,"size_bytes":21750,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-agent2-conversations.md","type":"markdown","lines":273,"executable":false,"size_bytes":15682,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-agent3-expression-dna.md","type":"markdown","lines":291,"executable":false,"size_bytes":17025,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-ravikant-agent1-著作与系统思考.md","type":"markdown","lines":387,"executable":false,"size_bytes":21635,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"examples/naval-perspective/references/quality-validation.md","type":"markdown","lines":120,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5806,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/extraction-framework.md","type":"markdown","lines":151,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4969,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/skill-template.md","type":"markdown","lines":110,"executable":false,"size_bytes":3412,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-c0a16cba1b8e4b449a5ee937a4598b3a","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":185,"end_line":null},"finding":"SKILL.md (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"Output: `SKILL.md` (main file) + research source index appended at the end.","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3759e6a4effbd89fa5b6fc80754a6923d55bc99fda186e8e597107f2cd346b04","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":185,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA1","finding_id":"finding-04a50b1844164da6b749b2047901f3e7","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Self-Modification","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":233,"end_line":null},"finding":"Update SKILL","explanation":"Skill modifies its own code, configuration, or behavior at runtime. Self-modification enables an agent to escalate privileges, disable safety constraints, or install persistent backdoors.","remediation":"Prevent the skill from modifying its own code, SKILL.md, or configuration files. Treat skill files as read-only at runtime.","code_snippet":"1. Read existing SKILL.md, note last research date\n2. Only launch Agent 2 (latest conversations) + Agent 5 (latest decisions) + Agent 6 (timeline update)\n3. Compare new info with existing content — strengthen, update, or add\n4. Update SKILL.md incrementally, don't rewrite entirely\n\n---\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7998d0e4ecc4a807bbc60abf0c076946e892f0d093c4d8396ff5d09f46c87275","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":233,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-f04c7628724b401e87b78349e3526bca","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":60,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":60,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-f04c7628724b401e87b78349e3526bca","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":198,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes a malicious update.","remediation":"Pin the version: npx @scope/server@1.2.3","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI16","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"2b5664f2a936abba4141331e7b3e83205cce617d2cea9af83aa306db07500782","occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":198,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-4d88ccfdf64c401ca2dfad116502a62f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":65,"end_line":77},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README suggests invoking the skill with phrases like “帮我做一个…Skill”, “用芒格的视角帮我分析…”, and “切换到Naval…”, but it does not define a specific trigger set or clarify when these phrases should or should not activate the skill. Because these are ordinary conversational phrases rather than constrained commands, they risk overlapping with normal chat and causing unintended invocation.","remediation":"Document explicit trigger phrases or command formats, and add scope constraints or negative examples showing similar phrases that should not activate the skill. If activation is limited to a specific command palette or explicit skill-selection step, state that clearly in the README.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":65,"end_line":77}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-e59e2874e9b44fd1a1fc760e90a721d1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":6,"end_line":6},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger phrases are broad enough to activate on common language like 'make a skill for X' or 'distill X,' which can cause the skill to run unintentionally in unrelated contexts. Because this skill performs multi-step research and file creation, accidental activation can lead to unexpected external lookups, unnecessary agent execution, and local artifact generation without clear user intent.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger phrases to explicit invocations such as 'use nuwa-skill to create a perspective skill for X' and require a confirmation step before any research or file operations begin. Add intent disambiguation rules so generic phrases do not activate the skill unless the user clearly requests this specific workflow.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":6,"end_line":6}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d2e208e02f384400a45297be68fa2b1b","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":41,"end_line":62},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs the agent to create a local directory structure immediately after confirmation, but the front matter does not warn users that local files and folders will be created and maintained. This can violate user expectations and lead to unauthorized writes in environments where filesystem changes are sensitive, persistent, or shared across projects.","remediation":"Add an upfront warning in the skill metadata and opening section stating that the skill will create and update local directories and files. Require explicit user consent for filesystem writes, scope all writes to a dedicated workspace, and provide a dry-run mode that previews paths before creating them.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":41,"end_line":62}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d0349fa36c2a464cb997552397eb6dad","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":56,"end_line":59},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill directs the system to download and store external source materials under local folders, but it does not disclose this data-handling behavior or define privacy boundaries. Storing articles, transcripts, and other sourced content can expose sensitive research targets, retain copyrighted or personal data, and create persistent local records the user did not knowingly approve.","remediation":"Disclose clearly that the skill may fetch, download, and persist external materials and metadata. Ask for explicit approval before downloading or storing content, minimize retained data, document retention rules, and prefer linking to sources over saving full copies unless the user opts in.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":56,"end_line":59}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-513440d9472c4c68a20d3f0c590a880f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":9},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger list includes broad, common analytical phrases such as asking whether a cost is reasonable or to think from first principles, which can cause the persona skill to activate outside clearly intended contexts. Because the skill then instructs the assistant to respond directly in-character and avoid meta-analysis, accidental activation can override normal assistant behavior and steer unrelated conversations into a forceful persona with its own behavioral biases.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger conditions to explicit invocations only, such as exact phrases like 'use Elon Musk perspective' or 'activate elon-musk-perspective'. Remove generic business-analysis phrases from auto-trigger logic, and require a confirmation step before entering roleplay when intent is ambiguous.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/SKILL.md","start_line":7,"end_line":9}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-bf16bea9d40b4cd2a2f7934ff8fa5898","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/SKILL.md","start_line":216,"end_line":221},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill prescribes a Chinese-specific output style and lexical constraints without requiring user preference or language negotiation. This can cause unwanted language switching or stylistic coercion, reducing user control and potentially interfering with higher-priority system or user instructions about language, accessibility, or tone.","remediation":"Make language and style adaptation conditional on the user's current language and explicit preference. Replace mandatory Chinese-output guidance with optional localization rules, and state that the assistant should preserve the user's language unless the user asks to switch.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/SKILL.md","start_line":216,"end_line":221}]},{"id":"SSD-1","finding_id":"finding-69040131569243379f350ca4726b3622","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"examples/naval-perspective/SKILL.md","start_line":18,"end_line":25},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly instructs the model to remain in character, speak in first person as Naval, and avoid meta-analysis except on an explicit exit command, while limiting disclaimers to the first activation. This can suppress ongoing safety transparency, make users more likely to mistake generated content for authentic authoritative advice, and interfere with the assistant's ability to surface uncertainty, boundaries, or corrective framing when needed.","remediation":"Remove the prohibition on meta-level clarification and allow the assistant to break character whenever safety, uncertainty, or policy compliance requires it. Keep attribution persistent and lightweight throughout the interaction (for example, periodic reminders that this is a simulated perspective), and state explicitly that user safety instructions and platform policies override role-play behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/naval-perspective/SKILL.md","start_line":18,"end_line":25}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-0b1db95b0a4044ebb262438cfcf6ac04","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"examples/naval-perspective/SKILL.md","start_line":245,"end_line":250},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill hard-codes Chinese output style guidance without clearly preserving user language preference, which can override normal conversational expectations and reduce reliability for non-Chinese users. This is not a direct security exploit, but it is a genuine policy/control weakness because prompt-level behavior is being constrained in a way the user did not request.","remediation":"Add an explicit rule that the assistant should mirror the user's language unless the user asks for Chinese. Reframe the section as optional style guidance (e.g. 'if responding in Chinese...') rather than a mandatory output constraint, and state that user preference takes priority over skill defaults.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/naval-perspective/SKILL.md","start_line":245,"end_line":250}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-f143614488ac42429d896f211a6f0786","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-agent3-expression-dna.md","start_line":1,"end_line":291},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file presents all descriptive and instructional content in Chinese, and does not indicate that users may choose another language or that the content is intentionally limited to a Chinese-speaking audience. Under the natural-language policy rule, forcing a specific language without user opt-in can be a locale-policy violation.","remediation":"Add a note that the content is intended for Chinese-language users, or provide a language selection/alternate version so users can opt into their preferred language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-agent3-expression-dna.md","start_line":1,"end_line":291}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-6a7d6ff54b574c6ea119eed7ecb1a0d9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-ravikant-agent1-著作与系统思考.md","start_line":1,"end_line":387},"finding":null,"explanation":"This markdown file presents all instructions and analysis in Chinese, which effectively forces a specific language/locale on the user. Under the policy, language constraints should either be optional for the user or clearly justified as region-specific; neither is stated here.","remediation":"Add a clear language/locale note explaining why Chinese is required, or provide a bilingual/multilingual option so users can choose their preferred language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/naval-perspective/references/naval-ravikant-agent1-著作与系统思考.md","start_line":1,"end_line":387}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-fa24df11750c4204b7c31db069fb7fc6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/skill-template.md","start_line":1,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file presents the skill template entirely as a Chinese-language interaction pattern and does not offer any user language choice or opt-in. Under the policy, forcing a specific language or locale without user selection is a natural-language policy concern.","remediation":"Document that language should follow the user's preference, or explicitly provide multilingual/locale selection behavior. If the template is intended only for a Chinese-language deployment, state that limitation and its justification clearly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/skill-template.md","start_line":1,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-c4f463fb61d5469498a3c67a580dee86","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"references/skill-template.md","start_line":14,"end_line":15},"finding":null,"explanation":"The trigger examples are broad enough to activate on ordinary conversational phrasing such as asking to think from someone's angle, which can cause the skill to take over without clear user intent. In this skill's context, unintended activation is more concerning because activation leads to strong roleplay and identity-mimicking behavior, increasing the chance of misleading outputs or bypassing the user's expected interaction mode.","remediation":"Narrow the trigger conditions to explicit invocation phrases only, such as requiring the skill name or a clearly delimited command. Remove generic phrases like 'X 会怎么看' or '切换到 X' unless combined with confirmation, and add a disambiguation or user-confirmation step before activating roleplay behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/skill-template.md","start_line":14,"end_line":15}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-7a1863f4df714b8494e906a4f9691c50","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.72,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":26,"end_line":204},"finding":null,"explanation":"Most operational instructions, examples, and methodology are provided only in Chinese, while the English section is a short summary directing readers back to the Chinese content. This can amount to a language-access limitation because users are not offered an equivalent language choice for the full instructions.","remediation":"Provide a complete English version of the README or explicitly state the supported language(s) and that the primary documentation is Chinese-only, so users can opt in knowingly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":26,"end_line":204}]},{"id":"SQP-1","finding_id":"finding-5239be0c71a64c71959a54f2e2d54f94","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"README.md","start_line":110,"end_line":120},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README states “输入一个名字后” and the English summary says “Input a name,” but it does not specify whether any name, any public figure, or only certain supported subjects are valid. This leaves the activation condition underspecified and can make it unclear when the skill should run versus when a user is merely mentioning a person in conversation.","remediation":"Specify the acceptable target scope explicitly, such as 'public figures only' or a required command structure, and include examples of non-triggering mentions or unsupported names.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"README.md","start_line":110,"end_line":120}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-3de3bcaafad34b4c86e7be79afd6d964","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/Elon-Musk-思想体系调研-20260404.md","start_line":1,"end_line":315},"finding":null,"explanation":"SQP-3 applies to all file types and covers language or locale policy violations. This markdown file presents all instructions and analysis in Chinese, but nowhere indicates that Chinese is required, optional, or user-selected, which can amount to forcing a specific language without opt-in.","remediation":"Add a brief note at the top stating the intended language/locale and, if applicable, that alternative language versions are available or can be provided on request.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/Elon-Musk-思想体系调研-20260404.md","start_line":1,"end_line":315}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-153730262d764b17a3531ec3b1e54656","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"examples/elon-musk-perspective/references/马斯克决策模式与行为分析-20260404.md","start_line":1,"end_line":324},"finding":null,"explanation":"该文件是自然语言参考资料，内容从标题到正文均固定为中文，未见提供其他语言选项、用户选择机制，或说明其仅适用于中文读者/中文环境。根据语言/locale 政策，强制单一语言而无用户 opt-in 可能构成自然语言层面的组织政策问题。","remediation":"在文档开头补充语言适用说明，如“本资料当前为中文版本”，并提供或指向其他语言版本；若技能仅面向中文场景，也应明确注明语言范围和理由。","code_snippet":null,"intent":